{"ts": 1784362972.4942749, "event": "finish", "summary": "Held the entire episode: this SHORT never showed a genuine wrong-direction signature -- after the brief early flat/dip in the first ~2 minutes it built a near-monotonic favorable run from roughly +10 to +225pts by t=45m, with giveback off the running peak staying in the single-to-low-double digits almost every frame and repeatedly making new highs. Detector fires (KMDR/HA/PROPP) flipped against the position multiple times near local peaks, but price never actually reversed enough to erode the thesis, so bailing on any of those fires would have been cutting a winner short. Next time I'd watch for a giveback that keeps expanding across several consecutive frames (not just one against-fire) combined with a failure to make a new high within a few minutes -- that combination, not a single indicator flip, is what would signal a real trend exhaustion worth bailing on.", "exit_frame": null, "n_commits": 46}
